\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Retrieval and reranking performance. Overall results use the supplied task-weighted Dataset=Average rows (dataset scores weighted by task count); no new aggregation. Bold/underline mark best/second distinct value within each model, retriever, and metric (ties retained). R@k denotes Recall@k, the fraction of relevant skills recovered within the top k positions. Average is the task-weighted mean across test instances, equivalently dataset scores weighted by task count. Exact-zero metrics are shown as -. Baseline retrievers select all 50 candidates; raw-baseline F1 is loaded-set F1, not F1@5. These tables do not constitute controlled common-candidate method comparisons.}}{1}{}\protected@file@percent }
